      "But when Mariam was only about three, her dear mama and papa died, just days apart. A kind uncle took Mariam in. She missed her parents very much, but she never stopped believing that God was close. Even when she was small, she began to fast on Saturdays to show her love for the Blessed Mother.",
      "Mariam loved to pray, and she said the Holy Spirit talked to her heart like a gentle friend. She would listen carefully and do whatever it whispered. Some people were surprised such a little girl could be so peaceful — but Mariam simply said, 'The Holy Spirit tells me what to do.'",
