      "Nathanael was doubtful. 'Can anything good come from Nazareth?' he asked. Philip did not argue. He just smiled and said four wonderful words: 'Come and see.'",
      "Nathanael came — and saw! When he met Jesus, his whole life changed. Philip had given his friend the greatest gift by simply inviting him. That is how it so often works with Jesus: we do not need fancy speeches, just a friendly 'come and see'.",
      "Philip became one of the twelve apostles. He walked with Jesus for years, watching the miracles and learning the lessons of the kingdom. He was one of the first, boldest and most faithful followers.",
      "At the last supper, Philip made a beautiful request. 'Lord,' he said, 'show us the Father, and we shall be satisfied.' And Jesus answered: 'Whoever has seen me has seen the Father.' Philip learned that Jesus himself was the face of God's love.",
