      "One of the men she refused was Quintianus, the powerful governor of Sicily. “Marry me, or else!” he demanded, red with anger. Tradition tells us he had poor Agatha arrested and thrown into a dark prison. “Give up your Jesus!” he shouted through the bars. “Never,” whispered Agatha.",
      "The governor tried to break her courage with cruel punishments that hurt her terribly. But Agatha prayed through every tear, holding onto Jesus with all her strength. Then, in the darkness of her cell, tradition tells us something wonderful happened. St Peter himself appeared, glowing softly, and comforted her like a kind father.",
      "Strengthened by the vision, Agatha stood firm to the very end. Around the year 251, she passed away peacefully in her prison cell, whispering a prayer. She was free at last, flying straight to the Jesus she loved more than any earthly prince. Heaven welcomed its brave little daughter home.",
